* Responses to a minor-suit opening

Booklet section "RESPONSES TO A 1C OR A 1D OPENING": bidding at the one level is
up-the-line, responder needs four cards to raise 1!d but five to raise 1!c (one
fewer will do in a pinch in a competitive sequence), 2NT is 13--15 game forcing,
3NT is 16--18, and there is no forcing minor-suit raise. Since every suit above
clubs is reachable at the one level, the only *true* two-over-one below 1!d is
2!c over a 1!d opening (clubs has no one-level route once diamonds is opened);
jump shifts into a major over a minor opening are not modeled here (the booklet
does not restate them for minors, and by symmetry with the major-suit ones they
would need the same negated-support handling -- see NOTES.md #6). The 2NT/3NT
raises are for hands without an unshown 4-card major, so that a 1-level major
response is chosen first when both apply. The 1NT response excludes the
single-raise length (5+ clubs, 4+ diamonds), so a 6--9 hand with a fit raises
instead of bidding notrump (the two used to share a range and 1NT, listed first,
always won).

Two hands had no call at all (NOTES.md #C5): the invitational 3=3=3=4 hand over
1!c (no four-card suit to bid at the one level, too strong for 1NT, too weak for
2NT), which raises to 3!c with four clubs -- the booklet's "one fewer will do in a
pinch" -- and a hand too strong for the 16--18 3NT with no four-card major, which
the booklet leaves without a natural route (there is no forcing minor raise); it
starts with 3NT, and slam exploration from there is left to judgment.

** After 1!c

1C-
1D = {prio:2} F, 6+ hcp, 4+!d
1H = {prio:2} F, 6+ hcp, 4+!h
1S = {prio:2} F, 6+ hcp, 4+!s
2N = F, 13--15 hcp, not 4+!h, not 4+!s
1N = NF, 6--9 hcp, not 5+!c
2C = 6--10 hcp, 5+!c
3C = 5+!c and 10--12 hcp or 4=!c and 0--3!d and 0--3!h and 0--3!s and 10--12 hcp
3N = 16+ hcp, not 4+!h, not 4+!s

** After 1!d

1D-
1H = {prio:2} F, 6+ hcp, 4+!h
1S = {prio:2} F, 6+ hcp, 4+!s
2C = {prio:1} F, 10+ hcp, 4+!c
2N = F, 13--15 hcp, not 4+!h, not 4+!s
1N = NF, 6--9 hcp, not 4+!d
2D = 6--10 hcp, 4+!d
3D = 10--12 hcp, 4+!d
3N = 16+ hcp, not 4+!h, not 4+!s
